1595:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"6dc808cd000a19b8f897011d8e84ccb221320b9141c4538b5de95208b8a96a47\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review documentation and code consistency.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-docs\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"9aaa80a9426a04ea031a7feeb6cd409a236ca6493286bf50f3e5deed012009f7\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"Introduce the deep ManagedHostRun module with immutable spec/owner/claim, one-shot prompt capability, snapshots/events/live output, absolute deadline, cooperative cancel, exclusive terminal receipt, next-touch reconciliation, replacementSafe, retention and runtimeContinuation semantics. Silence alone never fails or restarts a run.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/runtime-artifact-registry.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/session-ownership-and-write-leases.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Persist and reconcile managed host-run lifecycle\",\"userSees\":\"用户运行 host_run_status 时看到同一个 runId 的 running/terminal 状态、deadlineAt、workerHeartbeatAt、providerProgress、replacementSafe 和 receiptDigest；静默不会显示为失败或触发新 run。\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Race multiple status, attach, cancel, and reconcile callers at the deadline; exclusive reconciliation and terminal creation must yield one immutable terminal receipt and all callers must converge on its exact digest.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Present missing, corrupt, partially-written, or identity-ambiguous runtime artifacts; the run must fail closed with honest residual unknown and replacementSafe false where cleanup cannot be proven, with no blind kill and no automatic replacement.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Race provider success against cancel and deadline expiry; exactly one authoritative terminal outcome wins, cleanup and residual facts are recorded, and replacementSafe becomes true only when the former execution can no longer write results or evidence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Keep a real provider fixture silent longer than the legacy first-output and caller-observation boundaries while its process remains alive; repeated next-touch status calls must keep the same run running, report worker liveness separately from provider progress visibility, and never restart it merely because output is absent.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Crash the worker after claim and before terminal publication, then exercise status before and at the finite absolute deadline; reconciliation must preserve the original identity before deadline and eventually materialize definite timed_out or failed terminal truth rather than wait forever.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Submit one managed provider run, observe immutable spec and owner plus a successful worker claim, then observe monotonic snapshots and events ending in exactly one completed terminal receipt whose digest is returned by status; proves the durable lifecycle from submission to terminal truth.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Terminate the original caller after submission while the provider remains active, then query the returned runId from a new caller and observe the same execution continue to completed without a second provider spawn or replacement; proves caller lifetime is not run lifetime.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Make foreground host_run submit-and-attach over the durable run, add detach submission with claim handshake, bounded host_run_status long-poll, idempotent host_run_cancel, and a hidden worker continuation. Keep text/json passthrough contracts and prompt secrecy.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/cli-engine.ts\",\"packages/main/src/cli/command-catalog.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/command-policy.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/registry.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-command-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-codex-command-boundary-execution-plan.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Expose submit, attach, status and cancel command surfaces\",\"userSees\":\"用户用 host_run --detach 得到 runId 后，可用 host_run_status --waitMs 最多等待 30 秒并用 host_run_cancel 幂等取消；前台模式仍显示实时输出，但调用方结束后相同 runId 可继续查询。\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Inspect process arguments, persisted terminal and evidence artifacts, and post-claim runtime files; prompt and capability plaintext must not appear in argv or durable receipts, one-shot inputs must be mode 0600 and removed after claim, and only bounded redacted projections or digests may remain.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Supply unknown, malformed, path-traversal, cross-project, or stale runId values to status and cancel; commands must reject without reading or mutating another run and without spawning any provider process.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Kill the foreground attaching caller while its managed worker is active, then attach from a new caller; the original run must remain observable and complete once, proving CLI watchdog runtimeContinuation cannot translate caller loss into provider cancellation.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Exercise waitMs at 0, 30000, and above 30000 plus a no-change interval; every call is bounded, values above the cap are rejected or capped explicitly, and a wait timeout reports the current non-terminal state without treating it as provider failure.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Call host_run_cancel repeatedly before claim, during execution, and after terminal completion; cancellation is idempotent, targets only the original run, and never creates a second terminal or changes an already authoritative terminal outcome.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Detached host_run returns only after the worker claim handshake with runId, running state, and deadlineAt; host_run_status --waitMs 30000 then long-polls that same identity and returns progress or its terminal receipt, while foreground host_run is submit-and-attach over the identical durable run.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Text and JSON foreground attachment preserve existing routing contracts: text host stdout streams once to stdout, JSON keeps stdout to one result object while transcript streams to stderr, and provider usage and passthrough errors remain honestly represented.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Use POSIX process groups for TERM/KILL/reap/residual checks, fail before spawn on unsupported platforms, launch Codex with documented explicit stdin -, preserve provider usage parsing and configured timeout ceilings, and separate worker heartbeat from provider progress visibility.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/codex-review-leaf.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-process-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/provider-codex-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-003\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/tier-c-crosshost-quorum-execution-plan.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Supervise provider processes portably and honestly\",\"userSees\":\"用户看到 silent provider 保持 running 直到真实退出或绝对 deadline；取消/超时结果明确报告 TERM/KILL/reap/residual，Codex 执行使用 stdin '-' 且不会等待未关闭输入。\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Simulate PID or PGID reuse and a mismatched spawn fingerprint at reconcile time; the supervisor must not signal the ambiguous process, must record residual unknown and replacementSafe false, and must not authorize automatic replacement.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Keep the provider silent but alive until its explicit configured absolute deadline; silence alone must not signal or fail it, while the actual deadline must still trigger bounded group cleanup and timed_out terminal truth.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Make stdout and stderr flood, split structured usage records across chunks, and close passthrough sinks asynchronously; supervision must remain bounded, not crash on EPIPE, preserve honest usage availability, and still release process and admission resources.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Exercise a provider leader that exits while a child remains plus a provider that ignores TERM; supervision must check the process group, escalate to KILL after the bounded grace period, reap, and report any residual honestly rather than treating leader exit as full cleanup.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"On an unsupported non-POSIX platform seam, submission must fail before spawn with an explicit unsupported-platform result; no partially supervised child or misleading replacementSafe true may be produced.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"For observable and unobservable providers, snapshots must keep workerHeartbeatAt distinct from lastProviderProgressAt and providerProgressMode; a fresh worker heartbeat cannot be used as evidence of provider output or completion.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"On POSIX, launch a fixture that creates a provider process tree in its own group, then complete or cancel it and prove TERM or KILL, reap, and residual probing leave no surviving group member; terminal records the exact cleanup facts.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Launch the Codex adapter through its documented exec stdin sentinel, write the prompt to stdin and close it, then preserve terminal usage parsing and configured provider timeout semantics; proves the managed adapter uses codex exec ... - rather than an undocumented implicit prompt path.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"All provider-process launch sites must acquire the same bounded slot registry even when usage accounting is disabled. Preserve ledger fail-closed behavior, candidate-spec streaming/retention semantics, and explicitly classify remaining migrated/unmanaged execution surfaces.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/src/core/provider-process-admission.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/autopilot-executor.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/codex-review-leaf.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/lattice-dispatch.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/candidate-spec-routing.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/candidate-spec-routing-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/host-run-usage-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/provider-process-registry-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-004\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-llm-usage-ledger-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/multi-host-keyword-candidate-spec-routing-execution-plan.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Enforce shared provider admission independent of usage-ledger mode\",\"userSees\":\"即使 LATTICE_USAGE_LEDGER=0，并发超过 cap 的跨 Provider 启动仍在 spawn 前被明确拒绝并列出占用 run；已有 usage 与 candidate routing 输出格式保持不变。\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Enumerate production provider spawn call sites and prove each is either routed through the shared admission boundary or explicitly classified legacy_unmanaged with no gate claim; a new direct spawn path must make the contract test fail.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Corrupt, truncate, or replace slot metadata during acquire and release races; admission must fail closed or reclaim only after re-verifying ownership, and a stale releaser must never unlink a newer holder slot.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Force ledger append failures for allowed, blocked, and final records while provider admission is active; no output may claim a row was recorded when it was not, but slot acquisition and release must still be enforced independently.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Race more contenders than the cap against fixed numbered slot creation, then crash a holder; atomic admission permits no oversubscription, dead or orphaned slots are reclaimed under their documented rules, and an old but live holder is never reclaimed by age alone.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Lower the configured cap while high-index runs are live and then release them; existing holders drain without deletion, new admissions use only the lowered range, and token-guarded late release cannot delete a reclaimed and re-acquired slot.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Feed candidate-spec and usage parsing streams with valid candidates, chunks over 64 KiB, post-candidate overflow, and no first candidate; live per-chunk output remains intact while retained candidate state follows discard-all overflow and null-first-output rules exactly.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"With LATTICE_USAGE_LEDGER disabled and the shared cap set to one, start one long provider run and attempt a second launch from every migrated provider surface; exactly one holds admission and every concurrent launch site refuses pre-spawn until the slot is released.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"With the ledger enabled, provider admission remains the same while hard-budget decisions, blocked rows, final provider usage, and append failures retain their existing fail-closed and diagnostic-honesty semantics.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"cross_host_review retains snapshot/policy/redacted-env/structured-verdict ownership but delegates execution to ManagedHostRun under the privileged cross-host-verdict profile, attaches to terminal truth, validates verdict shape, and preserves existing timeout policy ceiling and fail-closed semantics.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/codex-review-leaf.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/cross-host-review.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/cross-host-review-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-005\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/review-assurance-floor-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/tier-c-crosshost-quorum-execution-plan.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Route cross-host review through managed execution\",\"userSees\":\"cross_host_review 仍返回原有 paired host verdict 与 jointDecision；其 host-B 结果新增可追溯 managed run receipt，且既有 policy timeout ceiling、blocked/error 文案不变。\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Try to bypass the privileged profile with a caller-supplied command, cwd, environment, output path, or verdict binding; cross_host_review remains owner of snapshot, policy, redacted environment, and verdict validation, and ManagedHostRun executes only the opaque approved profile.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Race material drift and cancellation after submission but before verdict persistence; stale or cancelled terminal output cannot be submitted as a current host verdict, and the joint decision remains blocked.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Prove cross_host_review no longer owns a second direct Codex spawn or kill stack by a source-contract test that fails if production execution bypasses ManagedHostRun.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Return malformed JSON, schema-invalid verdicts, a mismatched material hash, empty output, and abnormal provider exit; each must synthesize the existing blocked host-B verdict and fail closed while retaining only bounded digest or redacted diagnostics.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Exercise configured cross_host_review timeout ceilings and bounded attempts at their exact boundaries; migration to ManagedHostRun must preserve the existing ceiling, attempt count, and joint-decision behavior while replacing only execution supervision.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Keep Codex silent but alive inside the policy ceiling; cross_host_review must report the managed run as active rather than converting silence into codex_review_no_parseable_verdict before the configured deadline.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Run cross_host_review through the privileged managed profile with a fixed material snapshot and valid structured Codex verdict; it must attach to the managed terminal receipt, validate the verdict, submit the host-B result, and preserve an agreeing joint pass without exposing raw provider output.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"End the cross_host_review caller while its provider is still working, then resume by the managed run identity; the same review completes and is consumed once, with no duplicate Codex launch and no verdict loss caused by the caller boundary.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Extend dispatch/reviewer evidence contracts with a two-phase managed-review protocol. The provider reviewer writes a profile-bound evidence proposal (pass or findings plus truthful read evidence) into the run evidence journal; it never calls final review_pass_set/finding_add before terminal. After successful terminal seals the journal, a mechanical importer verifies exact story/reviewRun/lane/provider/prompt-envelope/material/terminal bindings and imports the provider-authored proposal without letting the controller change its verdict or impersonate the reviewer. Register the new gate-consumed managed receipt/composite evidence class in the shared Proof Admissibility artifact/intake/evaluator contract as well as process-fact registry. Raw CLI, controller-authored substitutes, and heuristic time-window ledger matches cannot satisfy managed evidence; structured degraded decisions remain explicit.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/src/core/managed-review-evidence.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/managed-review-evidence.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/evidence/admissibility/index.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/finding-verify.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/proof-admissibility-gates.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/proof-admissibility.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/review-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/finding.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/review-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/story-dispatch.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-review-evidence-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/proof-admissibility-registry-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/review-pass-discard-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/review-run-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-006\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/review-assurance-floor-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/review-run-binding-race.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Bind formal reviewer evidence to exact managed receipts\",\"userSees\":\"CLI reviewer 的 provider-authored pass/finding proposal 在该 run 成功终态并密封后被机械导入；精确 receipt 匹配会被 REVIEW gate 接受，而 raw CLI、controller 代写、未终态、伪造、陈旧、跨 Story/lane/provider 的 evidence 会被拒绝并给出具体 remediation。\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Controller non-impersonation E2E: after provider proposal creation, attempt every controller-supplied verdict, note, finding, evidenceState, reviewer identity, readManifest/readLog or provenance override and attempt direct controller final review_pass_set/finding_add as the managed reviewer; the importer exposes no such override surface, rejects altered bytes or identity, preserves the provider-authored proposal exactly, and never records the controller as reviewer.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Tamper each bound field independently, forge runId/terminal/proposal/journal digests, append or truncate journal bytes, swap receipts across story/reviewRun/lane/provider/prompt/material, or replay stale material; every variant is rejected by both import admission and REVIEW consumption while the byte-authentic control is accepted.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Shared-evaluator mutation contract: delete or bypass the shared Proof Admissibility intake/evaluator call at either import-time or REVIEW-gate consumption, hard-code an allow result, introduce a managed-review-only registry or parallel evaluator, or diverge a canonical reason code; the source/registry contract and mutation smoke must fail for every mutant, proving both boundaries consume one registry/intake/evaluator instead of mirrored special cases.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Submit raw bash plus provider CLI output, usage-ledger rows, matching provider/time-window metadata, controller-authored proof-looking fields, main/implementer evidence, or an unsealed provider proposal as the managed composite evidence; none may satisfy import, review_pass_set/finding provenance, REVIEW assurance or gate evidence, and each refusal uses a registered canonical remediation reason.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:3\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Race proposal publication, terminal creation, journal sealing and import while attempting a late proposal replacement; import cannot begin before the successful exclusive terminal covers the final proposal and journal digests, post-seal writes are rejected or integrity-invalid, and exactly one immutable provider-authored evidence identity can become gate-consumed.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:4\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"A missing terminal, pre-terminal proposal, failed/cancelled/timed_out/nonzero terminal, incomplete or ambiguous cleanup, missing proposal, or multiple proposals must receive the matching canonical Proof Admissibility refusal and import no ReviewPass/Finding; diagnostic or degraded evidence remains explicit and cannot upgrade to normal managed assurance.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"After a valid import, change materialHash, storyFilesHash, head lineage, prompt envelope, review round, lane policy, provider binding, proposal bytes or journal bytes; both a fresh import attempt and REVIEW-gate revalidation must fail closed through the shared evaluator with the same canonical stale/integrity/consumer reason family rather than trust a persisted boolean.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Replay the same authentic runId/receipt and race two importers; import is idempotent and converges on one exact ReviewPass or finding set with unchanged provider reviewer/read provenance, while a different receipt cannot supersede or rewrite the already imported provider proposal.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Native-host reviewer lanes retain their existing signed ReviewRun/pass/finding path, while an explicitly configured degraded-single-host result remains local and non-authority, names the absent managed composite evidence, and is never relabeled as provider-authored managed or two-host assurance.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:3\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"E2E pass path: the dispatched provider reviewer, while the managed run is active, authors exactly one immutable profile-bound proposal containing its pass verdict, registered reviewer identity, truthful readManifest/readLog, and exact story/reviewRun/lane/provider/prompt-envelope/material bindings; it writes no final ReviewPass. A successful terminal exclusively seals the proposal and append-only journal digests before managed_review_evidence_import accepts only the runId/receipt, and the importer creates the existing ReviewPass without changing verdict or authorship while preserving reviewer, lane, reviewRun and read provenance; the REVIEW gate accepts that exact current composite evidence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"E2E finding path: the provider reviewer authors immutable findings and read provenance in one sealed proposal, successful terminal precedes import, and the mechanical importer reproduces each provider-authored finding exactly with its reviewer/reviewRun/lane/read provenance; verified open high or critical findings remain visible to the normal REVIEW blocking predicates and cannot be replaced by a controller-authored pass.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"E2E admissibility path: import-time admission and later REVIEW-gate consumption both resolve the managed receipt/composite evidence through the same shared Proof Admissibility artifact registry, intake normalization, evaluator, producer/scope/claim/consumer/material policies, and canonical reason-code vocabulary; an authentic control receives the same admissible classification at both boundaries.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Test background continuation beyond caller lifetime, silent-but-live runs, worker crash with deadline reconciliation, cancellation races, process-tree cleanup, slot contention with ledger off, candidate overflow, forged/stale receipts and protected timeout preservation. Document operator status/cancel/recovery, legacy_unmanaged classification, trust boundary and rollout compatibility.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-suite-smoke.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"packages/main/src/core/runtime-artifact-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/doctor.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-suite-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-007\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Add adversarial coverage, observability, migration docs and rollout controls\",\"userSees\":\"文档与 doctor 清楚解释 30 秒是单次等待上限、静默不是失败、绝对 deadline 如何收敛、何时 replacementSafe；一条聚合 smoke 显示 managed host-run 全链路 PASS。\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"The integrated regression matrix includes silent-but-live execution beyond the former ten-minute observation boundary, worker crash, process-tree TERM-resistant cleanup, ledger-off slot contention, candidate overflow, async EPIPE, and no-output cases; each asserts no duplicate restart and finite terminal convergence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"The receipt negative-control matrix rejects forged, stale, cross-story, cross-lane, altered-journal, raw CLI, and heuristic ledger evidence while accepting the exact authentic managed receipt; removing any binding check must make the suite fail.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"CLI watchdog tests prove runtimeContinuation applies only to declared managed continuation commands: caller idle or max boundaries detach observation without killing the provider, while unrelated commands and explicit configured subprocess deadlines retain their existing enforcement.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"A worker-crash real-process smoke plus next-touch reconciliation proves eventual failed or timed_out convergence, while a cancellation-race smoke proves one terminal; both expose runId, deadlineAt, terminal reason, residual and replacementSafe to operators.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Runtime retention removes expired prompt and live-output material under documented policy while preserving the bounded terminal receipt and evidence references needed for audit; doctor classifies missing or corrupt runtime artifacts without treating them as success.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Migration inventory labels every remaining provider execution surface managed or legacy_unmanaged, preserves protected provider and cross_host_review timeout ceilings, and documents unsupported platforms plus the same-uid local trust ceiling without claiming cryptographic or authority proof.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"An end-to-end real-process smoke submits a run, ends the caller boundary, observes the same run from a new caller with no duplicate spawn, and reaches explicit completed terminal truth whose exact receipt is accepted by the intended formal reviewer consumer.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Operator documentation and diagnostics show how to submit detached work, inspect bounded status, distinguish worker heartbeat from provider progress, cancel, interpret deadline and residual states, decide whether replacement is safe, and recover without restarting on silence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}}],\"description\":\"Implement the approved ManagedHostRun boundary for CLI-launched cross-provider agents: durable detached/foreground execution, bounded status and cancellation, absolute deadlines, process-group cleanup, honest orphan/replacement safety, ledger-independent shared admission, and exact managed-run receipt binding for formal reviewer evidence. This supersedes heuristic time-window provenance matching such as the inactive B-1be5 proposal; it does not manage native host subagents and must preserve legacy configured provider timeout ceilings.\",\"headHash\":\"d173d5fc56049da48de81ccc3b98ff14df0fbf07\",\"materialHash\":\"df9085d895a799e40b8d574c96e6fb828e8369c87574c6ac950910d1826f1e92\",\"phase\":\"REVIEW\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.full-task-context.v1\",\"scope\":{\"allowedCreate\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md\",\"packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/managed-review-evidence.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/provider-process-admission.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/managed-review-evidence.ts\"],\"allowedModify\":[\"docs/host-run-usage.md\",\"packages/main/src/cli-engine.ts\",\"packages/main/src/cli/command-catalog.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/agent-dispatch-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/autopilot-executor.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/codex-review-leaf.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/command-policy.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/config.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/evidence/admissibility/index.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/finding-verify.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/host-execution-readiness.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/lattice-dispatch.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/planned-steps-executor.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/prompt-role-contract-registry.ts\",\"pack