   { name: 'runtime:routine_validation_fresh_pass_reuse_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/validation-evidence-reuse', rationale: 'Routine validate reuses structured command PASS only when the complete versioned execution identity, current required-intent coverage, material/story-file hashes, clean worktree, trusted exact-or-metadata-only lineage, and stable double-read HEAD all match. Identity and child execution share one effective environment: launcher-only _, OLDPWD, SHLVL, and ambient Proofbound host/session/role identity keys are removed, PWD is bound to command cwd, Windows keys are case-insensitively canonicalized/deduplicated with explicit command.env overlays winning and executable identity resolved through the platform path envelope (drive/UNC or slash/backslash explicit paths stay cwd/path-bound; only bare commands search canonical PATH/PATHEXT), while POSIX stays case-sensitive and PATH/NODE_OPTIONS/CI/locale plus explicit overlays remain semantic. Every legacy, malformed, changed, dirty, or uncertain input falls back to real execution without rewriting evidence.', gateConsumer: 'lattice validate TEST evidence producer and story_advance TEST/DONE validation consumers' },
   { name: 'runtime:acceptance_topology_plan_dev_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/acceptance-topology + handlers/proofstory + handlers/transition-orchestrator', rationale: 'PLAN to DEV consumes one deterministic structural report over the verifier-signed complete coverage basis and normalized reference-only topology. The independent, default-observe proofStory.acceptanceTopologyGateMode changes admission blocking only; caller status, mode, authority, executable evidence, Story prose, and the legacy ProofStory dev gate mode cannot change status or diagnostics.', gateConsumer: 'transition-orchestrator PLAN to DEV structural gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:acceptance_rollout_dev_review_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/acceptance-rollout + handlers/proofstory + handlers/transition-orchestrator', rationale: 'DEV to REVIEW consumes the current signed flat-project rollout report and genuine full-3x2 cohort. All modes compute identical status and ordered diagnostics; only explicit enforce blocks. Rollback changes config only and never rewrites report history.', gateConsumer: 'transition-orchestrator DEV to REVIEW rollout gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:topology_critic_authority_verification', level: 'L2', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/topology-critic-receipt + handlers/proofstory', rationale: 'Topology CLI verification requires registered critic/scope-plan roles, signed current bindings, four-dimensional independence, and one-to-one exclusion approvals. Critic prose or verdict cannot promote partial/unsupported discovery, and the result has no lifecycle admission authority.' },
   { name: 'runtime:done_required_validation_done_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/done-required-validation', rationale: 'DONE consumes doneRequiredCommands only when a project opts in: missing config is advisory/non-blocking, malformed opted-in config fails closed, and fresh PASS evidence must match current material, storyFilesHash, policyHash, commandSetHash, per-policy receipt coverage/identity/status, and any explicitly configured self-host build-proof requirements.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canFinish DONE done-required-validation gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:declared_artifact_committed_check', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'handlers/story-advance', rationale: 'DONE gate blocks when a declared artifact path is uncommitted or git-ignored so deliverables are not silently dropped at git merge.', gateConsumer: 'story_advance DONE declared artifact committed gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:live_smoke_transcript_done_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/live-smoke-transcript-evidence', rationale: 'Live-smoke evidence remains optional for legacy stories, but when the canonical evidence/live-smoke-transcript.json exists its storyId, executed-command mode, actual result, and zero exitCode are consumed fail-closed so timeout, spawn-failure, write-only, malformed, cross-story, and non-zero transcripts cannot be laundered through delivery review or DONE.', gateConsumer: 'delivery_check_set and storyMachine.canFinish DONE gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:delivery_promise_outcome_done_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/delivery-promise-outcome', rationale: 'A total shared normalizer classifies each delivery docsPromise as verified, waived, unresolved, or delivery_promise_outcome_contradiction. delivery_check_set rejects contradictions before persistence; machine and DONE oracle consume the same result and fail closed on invalid or unresolved rows, while only missing-status legacy rows may use bounded compatibility inference.', gateConsumer: 'delivery_check_set and storyMachine.canFinish DONE gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:finding_evidence_state_review_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/advisory', rationale: 'REVIEW to TEST gate consumes Finding.evidenceState: only verified (or legacy missing-field) open critical/high findings block, while suspected and disproven findings are advisory; isFindingBlocking enforces this dimension for both the canPassReview guard and getGuardFailureReason.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:review_run_workspace_binding_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/review-run', rationale: 'REVIEW evidence consumers verify reviewRun.workspaceBinding before accepting findings or review passes: the binding hash must match, the binding must still match the current story signed workspace resolution, top-level headHash/materialHash must agree with the binding, and freshness/scope checks use signedWorkspaceRoot instead of metadataRoot.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:review_run_story_files_hash_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/review-run', rationale: 'REVIEW evidence consumers verify signed ReviewRun.storyFilesHash before accepting findings or review passes: review_run_start persists the top-level storyFilesHash, folds it into the review run signature, checks durable persistence, and allows unrelated whole-tree main drift only when current story-owned files still match.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:review_run_atomic_persistence_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/mkdir-lock + handlers/review-run + handlers/agent-prompt', rationale: 'Every Prompt Envelope producer, including review_run_start and Story-aware agent_prompt, shares one bakery-style unique-ticket transaction lock. Every acquisition owns a never-reused UUID ticket path; choosing markers establish total order, and stale reclaim removes only the exact dead acquisition path. Two reclaimers therefore cannot delete a replacement holder through fixed-path ABA. review_run_start nests no fixed-path Prompt Envelope lock, so Prompt Envelope and ReviewRun read-modify-write remain one serialized transaction across all producers.', gateConsumer: 'review_run_start durable Prompt Envelope/ReviewRun persistence consumed by storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST and quorum_submit admission' },
+  { name: 'runtime:review_execution_authority_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/native-review-attestation + core/native-review-evidence + core/managed-review-evidence + core/review-run', rationale: 'REVIEW accepts direct reviewer evidence only when its ReviewPass/Finding signature seals a one-shot Ed25519 invocation attestation issued by an externally registered host-adapter broker and bound to the exact story, agent, lane, ReviewRun, writer session, signed dispatch and adapter/host identity. Lattice stores only registered broker public keys and exposes no issuer CLI or local private-key fallback. Process ancestry is optional corroboration when observable, but a visible mixed Codex/Claude ancestry is an unconditional veto. Raw provider CLI calls, missing/forged/replayed/cross-context attestations, absence of an authority binding, and degraded-single-host local facts cannot borrow native authority. Without a registered broker integration, native direct evidence is advisory-only and formal review must use the managed path. The managed cross-provider path requires one successful cleaned terminal receipt, one exact provider proposal artifact, and exact provider-authored verdict/read-provenance fields revalidated at intake, idempotent replay, and REVIEW consumption.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate through collectReviewerEvidenceState shared revalidation' },
   { name: 'runtime:prompt_envelope_review_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/review-run', rationale: 'Enabled full-envelope reviewer roles require one integrity-verified content-addressed review-run Prompt Envelope whose story, role/lane, round, ReviewRun, HEAD, materialHash and storyFilesHash equal the signed ReviewRun. The envelope also binds the exact standard story-dispatch prompt bytes and the selected host render identity: Claude Code/CLI map explicitly to Claude and Codex/CLI map explicitly to Codex. A nonblank explicit unsupported provider is preserved as unknown and takes precedence over competing Codex/Claude environment inference; antigravity/agy, fake, unknown, or absent providers fail closed because they have no PromptHost render identity. Runtime-owned/global-thin, registry, and explicit full-asset hosts all bind the same canonical role-specific body-free bootstrap separately from the selected role-body render, so total input is honestly bootstrap plus exactly one selected body rather than a false byte-exact mirror claim. review_run_start refuses missing dispatch provenance, and later selected-host bootstrap drift invalidates the run. review_run_start delivers and records the exact assembledPrompt bytes, promptHash must equal the envelope digest, canonical runtime/role/task assembly is recomputed, ReviewPass signs the same envelopeId, and REVIEW/quorum consumers use the shared verifier. The assurance floor consumes signed host-verdict rounds; quorum_submit is the mechanical boundary that refuses to emit those rounds unless all eligible envelope-bound reviewer passes are current.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate and quorum_submit reviewer-pass admission boundary; review assurance floor consumes resulting host-verdict rounds' },
   { name: 'runtime:incremental_review_eligibility_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/impact-classification-policy + core/review-incremental-context', rationale: 'Conditional incremental review consumes one versioned impact policy and the canonical freshness classification. Only an integrity-verified same-lane PASS bound to a valid ReviewRun and Prompt Envelope can establish a baseline; prior-pass selection is cut off at the signed ReviewRun startedAt (equal timestamps fail closed) so later metadata-only reviewer passes cannot rewrite an older envelope eligibility digest. The model-relevant TaskContext digest treats only TEST as equivalent to its REVIEW producer phase, preserving the exact digest produced by REVIEW across the mandatory REVIEW-to-TEST transition; DEV, DONE, DISCARDED, and malformed or unknown phases remain distinct and fail closed, as do title, description, priority, checklist, verification intent, and scope mutations. v1 allows no-material drift or fully Story-intent-bound pure fixture deltas, while unknown, docs, implementation, contract, authority, policy, dependency, dynamic, parse, rename, deletion, and incomplete fixture closure fail closed to full with stable reason codes.', gateConsumer: 'review_run_start trusted Prompt Envelope assembly and verifyReviewRunPromptEnvelope REVIEW/quorum/DONE/done_prepare admission chain through collectReviewerEvidenceState' },
   { name: 'runtime:prompt_role_body_rollout_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/prompt-role-contract-registry', rationale: 'Exactly five active REVIEW lanes have independent versioned rollout flags. review_run_start resolves a content-addressed byte-exact legacy role body or modular role body. Every supported host mode binds both the same role-specific body-free bootstrap and selected body, making total model input explicit. Mechanically, the actual package-registry resolver, global sync, and explicit full-asset renderer all return that bootstrap; review_run_start then supplies exactly one selected body

. REVIEW/quorum reconstruction rejects mode, role, body, bootstrap, host, or assembled-prompt substitution. Compatibility and retired roles cannot enable modular envelopes.', gateConsumer: 'review_run_start assembly, verifyCurrentReviewerDispatchBinding, verifyReviewRunPromptEnvelope, REVIEW gate, and quorum_submit admission' },
   { name: 'runtime:prompt_role_evidence_eligibility_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/prompt-role-contract-registry', rationale: 'The frozen 16-role Prompt Role Contract registry is the canonical role-status source. Only active canonical REVIEW roles can create or count ReviewRun/finding/pass evidence; compatibility and retired roles remain prompt-readable for history/migration but cannot satisfy REVIEW or quorum. The assurance floor does not interpret reviewer roles directly: it consumes host-verdict rounds, and quorum_submit emits those only after this eligibility gate passes.', gateConsumer: 'review_run_start, reviewer-list, storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate, and quorum_submit reviewer-pass admission boundary' },
   { name: 'runtime:agent_dispatch_role_authority_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/agent-dispatch-registry', rationale: 'The typed agent dispatch registry is the sole authority for canonical types and aliases, allowed phases, identifier cardinality, prompt class, commit guidance, reviewer lane, evidence ownership, and permitted state-changing commands. Unknown or partial roles fail closed before prompt generation; mutation consumers deny reviewer/implementer privilege crossover.', gateConsumer: 'dispatch prompt admission and role-gated checklist/reviewer evidence mutation consumers' },
   { name: 'runtime:canonical_scope_path_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/scope-path-classifier', rationale: 'Scope paths are written and compared as one versioned repo-root-relative identity resolved against the configured source root. Absolute, traversal, ambiguous-base, encoded-separator, prefix-collision, symlink-escape, and malformed glob inputs fail closed with original/canonical/base/version/rule diagnostics; malformed legacy protected/excluded patterns block before broad allow matching. Legacy history is read without mutation behind an independent rollout flag.', gateConsumer: 'scope contract write/check, prewrite, REVIEW, TEST, and DONE scope gates' },
   { name: 'runtime:ast_semantic_anchor_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/scope-diff-pack', rationale: 'Semantic scope consumes versioned TypeScript compiler AST enclosing declarations over actual changed spans. Control flow and local variables never become anchors; parser/version ambiguity, declaration-kind drift, protected declarations, multi-anchor changes, rename, and whole-file +++ /dev/null deletion fail closed or require re-attestation. Diagnostics name the actual violating declaration with kind/range/version/rule/remediation. AST rollout is independent from path canonicalization and rollback never rewrites signed history.', gateConsumer: 'semantic scope REVIEW, TEST, and DONE gates' },
   { name: 'runtime:shared_gap_log_metadata_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/lifecycle-registry', rationale: 'B-META framework-audit findings and the separate gap_log provenance ledger are shared lifecycle metadata only when the complete canonical-writer HMAC receipt chain is contiguous and its head binds the current whole findings artifact. Genesis requires an absent/canonically empty parent artifact; committed non-empty legacy history must match exactly. Missing, reordered, edited, public-digest-recomputed, replayed, direct-edited, canonical-path-symlinked, arbitrary, and unknown metadata fails closed with digest/receipt/remediation diagnostics; a later gap_log cannot launder altered history. This is cooperative same-repository tamper evidence, not same-UID authorization. Scope, prewrite, guard, and done_prepare consume the same classifier.', gateConsumer: 'scope contract shared-metadata classifier and done_prepare clean-tree gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:story_files_hash_freshness_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/evidence-freshness', rationale: 'Freshness consumers may accept whole-tree materialHash drift only when both recorded and current storyFilesHash match, must emit an explicit re-attestation advisory for that drift, and must still reject story-owned file changes or legacy records without storyFilesHash through strict materialHash behavior.', gateConsumer: 'REVIEW/TEST/DONE freshness gates for review runs, verification evidence, review escalation records, and the review assurance floor DONE freshness gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:review_escalation_done_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/review-escalation', rationale: 'DONE consumes the review escalation evaluator: direct decision-doc edits are diagnostic only; first REVIEW round countable verified/legacy reviewer findings or a valid explicitlyConfiguredHighRiskPolicyRequires3x2 policy fact trigger full 3x2 host quorum or explicit degraded 3x1 fallback over the current material hash, and non-human degraded fallback must be backed by a fresh review_host_availability_probe proving reviewReadyHostCount below 2 canonical hosts with executionReadyHostCount diagnostics.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canFinish DONE review escalation gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:review_assurance_floor_done_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/review-assurance-floor', rationale: 'DONE consumes the review assurance floor evaluator over a config-resolved, language-neutral material-code policy: policy resolution fails closed on a malformed lattice.config.json (never degrading to a TS-only whitelist), the change set is classified through one hash-bound classification snapshot delegated to the shared classifier, snapshot freshness (embedded HEAD/materialHash/policyDigest vs the live tree and config) is re-verified at consumption and re-resolved on drift, and a git diff enumeration failure hard-blocks instead of being treated as an empty non-material change set. The same snapshot/classifier is shared with the repro-evidence-binding and ProofStory consumers. Material code diffs require at least one fresh local host-verdict round, failure signals make 3x1 local single-host rounds sticky, high-risk lifecycle/gate/local-assurance/process-fact material work requires 3x2 host quorum or explicit degraded 3x1 fallback, non-human degraded fallback must be backed by a fresh review_host_availability_probe proving reviewReadyHostCount below 2 canonical hosts with executionReadyHostCount diagnostics, docs-only formats are not overblocked, and local evidence never sets retired remote-completion fields or release readiness.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canFinish DONE review assurance floor gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:evidence_environment_gate_projection', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/evidence/environment-contract + core/done-required-validation', rationale: 'The DONE_REQUIRED lifecycle evaluator resolves a registered descriptor, re-normalizes raw invocation and receipt input at consumption time, verifies receipt/invocation digests, current freshness and executor-owned environment/executable identity, then projects through the existing Proof Admissibility consumer. Receipt-provided host/trust strings and callback-returned identities cannot grant producer independence; distinct-host quorum is fail-closed unsupported until a project-owned pinned-key, session-bound and revocation-aware registry exists. Diagnostic-only evidence stays non-gating and adapters never own lifecycle completion.', gateConsumer: 'evaluateDoneRequiredEvidence DONE_REQUIRED lifecycle gate through validateDoneRequiredEvidenceEnvironmentProjection' },
   { name: 'runtime:proof_admissibility_gate_diagnostic', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/proof-admissibility', rationale: 'Gate-facing consumers classify proof-looking artifacts through the shared proof admissibility contract before reporting strong proof, local evidence, diagnostics, or legacy audit material; warn mode emits scope/reason/remediation diagnostics, while enforce mode blocks only configured high-risk consumers such as DONE_REQUIRED, REVIEW review-assurance/quorum, HANDOFF proof refs, and AUTHORITY_GATE_DECISION. The admissibility waterline remains read-only diagnostic output and cannot grant release readiness.', gateConsumer: 'configured proof-admissibility high-risk consumers: DONE_REQUIRED, REVIEW review assurance/quorum, HANDOFF proof refs, AUTHORITY_GATE_DECISION; diagnostic waterline remains read-only' },
   { name: 'runtime:parent_roadmap_totality_claim_consumer', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/parent-roadmap-totality', rationale: 'Parent-roadmap summary and handoff claim consumers must block explicit full-roadmap wording unless the row-fact evaluator derives allRowsClosed=true and claimType=full-roadmap-claim; honest partial_parent_done wording remains allowed.', gateConsumer: 'parent-roadmap summary/DONE/handoff wording consumers' },
   { name: 'runtime:closeout_artifact_trust_boundary', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/closeout-trust', rationale: 'Metadata-only retention accepts only the exact closed scope-defining/closeout-evidence path set and cooperative local-runtime lineage carrying a registered writer label; it is not same-UID authentication and does not approve artifacts. The sole index exception is a mechanically verified REVIEW-to-TEST delta whose stable fields and review round are unchanged and whose only appended event has exact TEST/advance semantics. Local event user/session/agent/timestamp/branch strings are audit context and cannot grant retention. REVIEW-to-TEST and TEST-to-DONE share evaluateReviewVerdict for required currentReviewRound presence, reviewer presence, signed current-round run binding, opt-in lanes, quorum, and blocking findings; absent currentReviewRound never activates legacy unsigned-evidence compatibility at these lifecycle gates. DONE also independently re-runs REVIEW-to-TEST preflight facts. Artifact gate validation remains independent and lifecycle path recognition alone never grants admissibility.', gateConsumer: 'REVIEW scope freshness and TEST/DONE metadata-only retention gates' },
   { name: 'runtime:composite_scope_digest_review_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/closeout-trust', rationale: 'Signed ReviewScopeBinding and done_prepare validation reuse bind semantic scope acknowledgement content/provenance plus validated milestone ledger and slice plan; missing or changed digests require fresh review/re-attestation.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate and done_prepare validation-reuse gate' },
   { name: 'runtime:trusted_closeout_artifact_validation', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/closeout-trust', rationale: 'Before local lifecycle use, milestone ledger, slice plan, parent rollup, and persisted delivery context are runtime schema validated with ledgerHash, planHash, rollupHash, cross-story, and exact local-only claim-shape checks. Review-retention lineage does not replace any artifact gate validator.', gateConsumer: 'ProofStory lifecycle gates, REVIEW scope freshness, and TEST/DONE closeout consumers' },
   { name: 'flow-policy:review-pass', level: 'L4', category: 'flow-policy', owner: 'core/flow-fact-policy', rationale: 'Review pass is a signed no-blocker fact consumed by REVIEW to TEST gates.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate' },
   { name: 'flow-policy:review-pass-supersession', level: 'L4', category: 'flow-policy', owner: 'core/flow-fact-policy', rationale: 'Older stale review pass receipts are superseded by newer valid passes in the same lane; stale findings remain blocking.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate' },
   { name: 'flow-policy:finding', level: 'L4', category: 'flow-policy', owner: 'core/flow-fact-policy', rationale: 'Reviewer findings are signed blocker-state facts consumed by REVIEW gates.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate' },
   { name: 'flow-policy:review-run-boundary', level: 'L4', category: 'flow-policy', owner: 'core/flow-fact-policy', rationale: 'Current REVIEW PASS evidence counts when its bound reviewer run is material- and scope-fresh in the current round; id-recency (being the latest run on the lane) is NOT required. FINDING evidence keeps the latest-run binding so an open finding bound to a non-latest run still surfaces (kind-aware review-run binding; see review-run-binding-race.md).', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate' },
   { name: 'flow-policy:pass-only-normalization', level: 'L4', category: 'flow-policy', owner: 'core/flow-fact-policy', rationale: 'Pass-only low-severity reviewer findings normalize to signed review pass receipts instead of open findings.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate' },
   { name: 'flow-policy:review-round-iso-string', level: 'L4', category: 'flow-policy', owner: 'core/flow-fact-policy', rationale: 'reviewRound is an ISO 8601 string in signed findings and review passes.', gateConsumer: 'review signatures and storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate' },
   { name: 'flow-policy:express-verification-policy', level: 'L4', category: 'flow-policy', owner: 'core/flow-fact-policy', rationale: 'Express channel stories may intentionally skip PLAN verificationIntent and must render that exemption explicitly.', gateConsumer: 'validate verification coverage and story_review PLAN fast-path advisory gate' },
 ] as const satisfies readonly ProcessFactLevelEntry[];

